A51: USB line-state log, and touch-to-recovery.

1. sweet_usb.c (A51): boots 28-30 ran the DWC3 with the PHY powered, VBUS
   forced and the SM5713 MUIC switched to USB by the shim, yet the host saw
   no connect and DSTS stayed "disconnected". The PHY supplies are on
   (shim SPEEDY probe: L12/13/14CTRL 0xcc/0xec/0xf0 = 0.85/1.8/3.0 V). For
   the first minute after RUN_STOP, log HSP_TEST.LINESTATE (what the PHY sees
   on D+/D-), UTMI, HSP, DSTS and DCTL every 2 s: J means the pull-up is out
   and the path to the connector is the problem, SE0 means the PHY is not
   pulling up.
2. a5xelte_touch.c (A51): hold one finger in the top-left corner (grid
   x,y < 100) for 3 s to warm-reset into recovery with the shim's PMU
   INFORM2/3 + SPARE2/3 magic and SWRESET, which keeps pstore and the
   sweetlog ring (a Power+VolDown reset is a cold MPON and loses them). The
   hold is also checked in the worker loop, as a still finger may produce no
   events.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index df261d1..59ef9ba 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -865,6 +865,26 @@ ud_thread(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t wr __unused)
 		if ((++ticks % 30000) == 0) {
 			printf("SWEET USB: ue0 rx %llu tx %llu frames\n", ud.rx_frames, ud.tx_frames);
 		}
+#if defined(A51)
+		/*
+		 * Line state while running (first ~60 s, every 2 s): HSP_TEST
+		 * LINESTATE [21:20] is what the PHY sees on D+/D- (0 SE0, 1 J =
+		 * D+ high, 2 K). J with no host activity points at the USB-C
+		 * switch (SM5713 MUIC), SE0 at the PHY's pull-up (boots 28-30).
+		 */
+		if (ticks <= 60000 && (ticks % 2000) == 0) {
+			static vm_offset_t u;
+			if (u == 0) {
+				u = ml_io_map(USBCON_PA, USBCON_SIZE);
+			}
+			if (u != 0) {
+				uint32_t t = usb_rd(u, USBCON_HSP_TEST);
+				printf("SWEET USB: A51 t=%us LINESTATE %u HSP_TEST 0x%08x UTMI 0x%08x HSP 0x%08x DSTS 0x%08x DCTL 0x%08x\n",
+				    ticks / 1000, (t >> 20) & 3u, t, usb_rd(u, USBCON_UTMI), usb_rd(u, USBCON_HSP),
+				    dwc_rd(DSTS), dwc_rd(DCTL));
+			}
+		}
+#endif
 		ud_sleep_ms(1);
 	}
 }
diff --git a/bsd/dev/a5xelte_touch.c b/bsd/dev/a5xelte_touch.c
